notify-senechal false FAIL, 2026-07-27 01:16, found by wtul-batch run 24 (first use from a wtul run). The guard filed the note correctly -- `scheduler -i senechal` committed 4586df8 and pushed it -- and then its own step-2 verification exited FAIL: "reported success but the note is not in .claude/FOCUS.md on senechal's remote". The note HAD landed. Re-ran the guard's own landed() check verbatim ~1 min later (probe = first 60 chars of the text, `git show @{u}:.claude/FOCUS.md | grep -qF "$probe"`) -> TRUE. senechal reflog shows one commit at 01:16:16 and no rewrite, so nothing changed under it. Most consistent with a fetch/ref-propagation race between `scheduler -i`'s push and the immediate `git fetch -q origin` + `git show @{u}:` that follows it -- the `ahead -eq 0` branch (line ~78) taken with an upstream ref that had the commit but a blob read that did not resolve. Worth a bounded retry (e.g. re-fetch + re-probe 2-3x with a short sleep before dying) rather than a single-shot check: this is the second false-negative this guard has produced in two days (the 2026-07-26 "are we ahead" one is named in its own comments), and a guard that cries wolf is one agents learn to talk past -- which is exactly the failure mode notify-senechal exists to prevent. Owner: realisateur (bin/notify-senechal.sh).
